{"id": "EUVD-2026-59653", "enisaUuid": "b9529388-603c-3a84-812a-10e874020faa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncan: ems_usb: validate CPC message lengths\n\nems_usb_read_bulk_callback() walks CPC messages packed in one USB\nreceive buffer.\n\nCheck that each declared message fits in the URB payload. Also require the\ntype-specific payload to cover the fields used by the CAN, state, error and\noverrun handlers.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T12:27:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:56:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c380a332e342b7d58c86c4f556cb0823b16a9b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb3cc8da8a2967c0f8e83d148fc6870b19fa32c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db5655287d78f00daf98888a520bb8da4d30126d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce8125566b1d0b0f16449407e014addf451804ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b9090717c7e2184e2c427bbcc752f295116ac1d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b23144c59c126beb4a7761a85a194ae0fe668a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df3ac2a672a5284441f120d486acabdd6740fc2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/02925f51377f2a42a6724f00549167499c9302e5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-596r-rcx5-45wx", "CVE-2026-74460"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09de1beb-c7bf-3737-960c-0ed717550659", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "702171adeed3607ee9603ec30ce081411e36ae42 <ce8125566b1d0b0f16449407e014addf451804ea"}, {"id": "0b1f6185-a913-3038-b91f-643a56aae5be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "0ddff3a4-1202-31dd-a84d-b8f5fc00021b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "702171adeed3607ee9603ec30ce081411e36ae42 <1c380a332e342b7d58c86c4f556cb0823b16a9b8"}, {"id": "65e2ea13-ec04-3891-bfc5-c8df9fea54f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "702171